      "title": "Group disability income",
      "narration": "Priya’s bakery pays the premiums for its short-term and long-term disability plans. Those premiums are a deductible business expense and are not income to the employees. Because the employer paid, benefits are taxable to the employee who collects them. If employees pay the premium themselves with after-tax dollars, benefits are tax-free. If they pay through a cafeteria plan with pre-tax dollars, the result is the same as employer payment: taxable benefits. Where premiums are shared, benefits are taxable in proportion to the employer-paid share. Some employers gross up the premium so employees pay tax on it now and receive tax-free benefits later.",
